# What follows the code of `-e` fills `ARGV` only when every word is a plain
# one: a brace list or a wildcard may become an option, which loads code. A
# list that makes the code of a second `-e` is read as the line it is, as the
# brace reading of any interpreter's code is: it finds what that code does.
